      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rossmoyne started as the 19th‑century Mill Dale before John Woltz renamed it, drawing Cincinnati businessmen to its quiet suburban charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rossmoyne_ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Located in Sycamore Township, one of Ohio’s first townships founded in 1803, Rossmoyne enjoys park access and ties to Cincinnati’s economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rossmoyne_ohio",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cunningham’s saw and grist mills, built by 1793, processed timber and grain, laying the groundwork for early homesteading in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rossmoyne_ohio",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Little Miami River valley around Rossmoyne offers rolling hills and fertile valleys that made the township ideal for early farming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rossmoyne_ohio",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Bechtold Park, a 22‑acre green space inside Rossmoyne, provides residents and visitors with a quiet place to stroll or picnic.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rossmoyne_ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
